# Docker Compose variables for a TENANT deployment — one tenant's
# user-facing half, pointed at a server deployment:
#
#   ./modules/backend/run_host_server.sh &   # leoserv; skip for text-only
#   docker compose --env-file config/tenant.env \
#       -f modules/backend/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/context/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/chat-ui/docker-compose.yml \
#       -f modules/monitoring/docker-compose.yml up -d --wait --pull always
#
# Despite the name, the tenant id itself is NOT in this file. Only values
# Compose needs before any container exists belong here: image tags,
# published ports, the project name. The tenant id and the server's address
# are what the application reads, so both live in config/custom.config — the
# id under [cltl.event.kombu] tenant.
#
# Unlike the other two roles, the values below are set rather than commented
# out: a tenant deployment shares a machine with the server deployment it
# talks to (or with another tenant), so it cannot simply take the compose
# files' defaults.

# Compose project name, and the name of the Docker network this deployment's
# modules join. MUST differ from the server deployment's (cltl-platform) and
# from every other tenant's — it is what keeps the two from sharing a network
# and colliding. Keep it in step with the tenant in config/custom.config.
CLTL_PROJECT=cltl-platform-tenant-a

# Seconds modules/context waits before starting, to keep it from opening a
# scenario that modules/emissor is not yet listening for — see
# modules/context's compose file. A tenant talks to a server-side emissor
# that has been up far longer than this, so 0 is reasonable here; the
# platform default of 10 is kept for a tenant brought up alongside a server
# in one go.
# CLTL_CONTEXT_START_DELAY=10

# Published host ports. Each must be free on this machine: 8001 is taken by a
# co-located server deployment's storage API, which is why the backend here
# is on 9001. A second tenant on this machine needs a different value for
# every one of these.
CLTL_BACKEND_PORT=9001
CLTL_CHATUI_PORT=8003
CLTL_MONITORING_PORT=8005

# Pin every image to one tag instead of :latest.
# VERSION=1.0.0
